 "extraction_notes": "Included only dark thermal CO2 methanation runs. Light-irradiated/photothermal entries, including the 12 h Ni@SiXNS-EtOH stability test under illumination and light data for Ni@SiO2 and Ni@Al2O3, were excluded as photothermal/out of scope. Text values override Fig. 5 bar readings. CO production rates were printed but there is no CO-rate field in the schema: Ni@SiXNS-H2O dark CO rate = 32.0 mmol gNi -1 h -1; Ni@SiXNS-EtOH dark CO rate = 5.1 mmol gNi -1 h -1; Ni@SiO2 dark CO rate = 193.70 mmol gNi -1 h -1. The paper states pressure qualitatively as atmospheric pressure; no numeric pressure was printed. Pristine calcined SiXNS was reported to show no activity under the same dark/light conditions, but no numeric rate or selectivity was given, so it was not entered as a quantitative performance record.",
